    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147">

                <pb facs="0349" n="329" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg329"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1120.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-10-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 10, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I enclose a copy of a recent correspondence
                    between this department and Mr. Burnley, her Majesty’s charge d’affaires, in
                    regard to an increase of the naval force of the United States on the lakes for
                    the present. I will thank you to make the needful explanations to Earl Russell
                    on the subject.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d147-a1.xml" xpointer="d147-a1"/>
            </div>
